# The p2_result npz are 14.8 MB each (99 MB for the set) and are deterministically regenerable:
# sweep_all.sh rebuilds the harness from named sources and re-derives them from the .pt weights,
# which are backed up on this laptop AND off it (kestrel_sigma_backup_20261021, 27 files,
# rclone-verified both ways). Committing them would bloat the repo permanently for no recoverable
# information. harness_provenance.sha256 pins which harness produced them.
results/
p2_results/   # the older name for results/; kept so a stale
              # checkout or an older sweep_all.sh cannot commit 99 MB
sweep_iso/
__pycache__/

# heads_iso/ holds two COPIES of views-hydranet files (vehicle.py, and tier2_remedies.py with only
# its EV path repointed). They are not this repo's code to carry — HARNESS_SOURCES.md records where
# they come from and their sha256 at time of use, which is what makes the run re-creatable.
heads_iso/vehicle.py
heads_iso/tier2_remedies_perhead.py
heads_iso/__pycache__/
